        "original_id": "e9914095-3474-5449-a7ae-26fb4e35ee89",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marcel Duchamp, Jiang Wen\n- Works: Prelude to a Broken Arm\n- Roles: painter, sculptor, chess player, writer, film actor, screenwriter, director\n- Art movements: Cubism, conceptual art, Dada\n\nFacts:\n- Marcel Duchamp was born on 28 July 1887 and died on 2 October 1968.\n- Marcel Duchamp was a French-American painter, sculptor, chess player, and writer.\n- Marcel Duchamp's work is associated with Cubism, conceptual art, and Dada, although he was careful about using the term Dada and was not directly associated with Dada groups.\n- Prelude to a Broken Arm is a 1915 sculpture by Marcel Duchamp.\n- Prelude to a Broken Arm consisted of a regular snow shovel with the title and \"from Marcel Duchamp 1915\" painted on the handle.\n- Jiang Wen was born on 5 January 1963.\n- Jiang Wen is a Chinese film actor, screenwriter, and director.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
